#
# File: filters.lut
#
# Database of available GMOS filters.
#
# This file contains a list of all the filters known to GMOS,
# whether fitted or not. Each time a new filter is purchased
# it should be assigned a barcode and added to this list.
#
# Surface curvature focus offsets come from measurements by Jeremy
# Allington-Smith, Isobel Hook and Stephanie Juneau on 7 July 2000.
# Effective wavelengths supplied by Isobel Hook on 24 January 2001.
# Names suggested by Inger Jorgensen on 31 January 2001.
#
# Surface focus offsets for order sorting filters were measured by
# Isobel Hook and Marianne Takamiya, Mar06 UT 2002.
#
# Surface focus offsets for GMOS-S order sorting filters were measured by
# Isobel Hook, May07 UT 2002.
# Commented out GMOS-S filters, they are no longer in GMOS-N, IJ, 2002oct14
# Added CaT GMOS-S, narrow band GMOS-N filters, IJ, 2002nov20
# Commented out CaT GMOS-S, added CaT GMOS-N, u' GMOS-N and GMOS-S, IJ, 2003jan14
#
# Added OIII, OIIIC, SII, HeII and HeIIC GMOS-N filters
# Commented out the rest of the GMOS-S filters, there were duplicated barcodes
# Edited the Empty filter cells so the barcodes matched the instrument and
# deleted the confusing commented out open slots with the wrong barcodes
#    - Kathy Roth 2009 June 03
#
# Moved the HartmannC and HartmannD focus masks from filter wheel 1
# to filter wheel 2 so filters in wheel 1 can be focused
#    - Kathy Roth 2009 July 31
#
# Added Z, Y GMOS-N filters - Kathy Roth 2010 May 11
#
# Added place holder for new Raman OVI 683.0 nm and corresponding 
# continuum filter under narrow-band filters and updated (commented)
# GMOS South information - Julia Scharwaechter 2017 Oct 11
#
# Added OVI and OVIC, Hartmann C and D are commented out 
# Eff. wavelength taken from lamda_0 measured in Test report_GMOS_S filter 20000035.docx
# - Julia Scharwaecher 2018 May 17
#
# Updated surface focus offset for OVI and OVIC - Julia Scharwaechter 2018 May 29
#
# Added user-supplied r+i filter 2018 Nov 7, surface curvature offsets still needs to be determined - Julia Scharwaechter
#
#                                 surface curvature
# name            barcodeId       focusOffset (microns)   effWavelength (nm)
#
# Empty filter cells - to be filled and barcodes reused
# open1-6 and open2-8 must not be filled as seqexec assumes these slots are open.
